{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDBVon93d9PNn81FVXX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed: `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so no grosz goes missing.\n\n**The bug:** `money.py` used `total // people` to get each share and threw away the remainder.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py:5`): it now uses `divmod`, which gives both the share and the remainder. The first `remainder` people each get one extra grosz. That means the shares always add up to the total, and no two shares differ by more than 1 grosz.\n\n**Tests** (`test_money.py`): I added two:\n- One checks the exact case you reported: `split_cents(100, 3) == [34, 33, 33]`.\n- One tries every total from 0 to 249 grosze with 1 to 7 people. It checks that the shares add up to the total and that the largest and smallest share are at most 1 grosz apart.\n\nBoth new tests failed before the fix. After it, all 5 tests pass (`python3 -m unittest`).\n\nOne thing to know: the extra grosze always go to the people listed first. If you'd rather spread them out another way, for example at random or by who ordered the most, that's a small change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":19171,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f079088-c722-44f7-af27-23489d4c1139","uuid":"e110fd56-f281-4fa1-9731-f3ba04f816e3","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:12:51.858Z","request_id":"req_011CggDBVZ9YmXAMiUNgvRog"}
